<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>FORSEE data centre press pilot</title>
<style>
:root{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#152631;background:#f5f7f5}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}header{padding:30px max(4vw,22px);background:#113b43;color:white}h1{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,39px)}header p{margin:0;max-width:900px;color:#cce0df;line-height:1.5}main{max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:24px max(3vw,16px)}.note{background:#e8f0ed;padding:14px 18px;border-left:4px solid #33786f;line-height:1.5}.controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(130px,1fr));gap:12px;margin:20px 0}.controls label{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:#51606a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}.controls select,.controls input{display:block;width:100%;margin-top:5px;padding:10px;border:1px solid #bccbc9;border-radius:6px;background:white;color:#152631;font:inherit}.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #d6e0dd;border-radius:9px;padding:16px}.card strong{font-size:26px;display:block}.card span{font-size:12px;color:#57696a}.bars{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin:12px 0}.barrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:70px 1fr 48px;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:8px 0;font-size:13px}.track{height:13px;background:#e8eeee;border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden}.fill{height:100%;background:#3f867e}.fr{background:#b77945}.small{font-size:12px;color:#617071}.results-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:10px}button{border:1px solid #adbfbc;background:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;cursor:pointer}article{background:white;border:1px solid #d6e0dd;border-radius:8px;padding:15px 18px;margin:9px 0}article h3{font-size:15px;line-height:1.4;margin:5px 0}article p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#344851;margin:8px 0}.tag{display:inline-block;padding:3px 7px;background:#ebf1ed;border-radius:4px;font-size:11px;margin-right:4px}.theme{background:#d8eee8}.theme.sov{background:#f1e4d3}.muted{color:#667}.snippet{border-left:3px solid #d8e4df;padding-left:10px;margin-top:10px}details summary{cursor:pointer;color:#266c69;font-size:12px}footer{font-size:12px;color:#586966;padding:20px 0}.hide{display:none}@media(max-width:850px){.controls{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.stats,.bars{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}@media(max-width:520px){.stats,.bars{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
 .newspaper-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:190px 1fr 95px;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:8px 0;font-size:13px}.newspaper-row .value{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.newspaper-row .label{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:600px){.newspaper-row{grid-template-columns:110px 1fr 85px}}
</style>
<header><h1>Data centres in the FORSEE press corpus</h1><p>France and Ireland · January 2022 to June 2025 · exploratory article screening. Search the article openings and short passages around data centre mentions. Counts are based on keyword rules and need qualitative checking.</p></header>
<main><div class="note"><strong>Read the categories cautiously.</strong> “Ecology” covers climate, emissions, water and sustainability; “energy” covers electricity and grid terms. “Sovereignty” uses explicit sovereignty, strategic autonomy and specific dependency terms. A theme is “near” when a keyword occurs within 500 characters of a data centre mention. Articles may be about other countries.</div>
<p class="small">The article list below is embedded in the file. For interactive filters, open the HTML file in Chrome, Firefox or Safari; some document previews disable JavaScript.</p>
<section class="controls">
<label>Country<select id="country"><option value="">Both</option><option>France</option><option>Ireland</option></select></label>
<label>Year<select id="year"><option value="">All years</option><option>2022</option><option>2023</option><option>2024</option><option>2025</option></select></label>
<label>Source<select id="source"><option value="">All sources</option></select></label>
<label>Nearby theme<select id="theme"><option value="">Any</option><option value="ecology_near">Ecology</option><option value="energy_near">Energy / grid</option><option value="sovereignty_near">Sovereignty</option><option value="ai_near">AI</option><option value="ecology_sovereignty">Ecology + sovereignty</option><option value="neither">Neither ecology nor sovereignty</option></select></label>
<label>Text search<input id="query" type="search" placeholder="e.g. Marseille, EirGrid"></label>
</section>
<section class="stats" id="stats">__INITIAL_STATS__</section><section class="bars"><div class="card"><strong>Articles by year</strong><div id="years">__INITIAL_YEARS__</div></div><div class="card"><strong>Nearby themes</strong><div id="themes">__INITIAL_THEMES__</div><div class="small">Themes overlap. Bars count articles, not mentions.</div></div></section>
<section class="card"><strong>Distribution by newspaper</strong><div id="newspapers">__INITIAL_NEWSPAPERS__</div><div class="small">Bars count articles in the current filter; percentages are shares of those matching articles. Outlet sizes in the underlying AI corpus differ.</div></section>
<div class="results-head"><h2 id="resultTitle">Articles (796)</h2><select id="sort" aria-label="Sort articles"><option value="mentions">Most data centre mentions</option><option value="newest">Newest first</option><option value="oldest">Oldest first</option></select></div><div id="results">__INITIAL_RESULTS__</div><button id="more" class="hide">Show more</button>
<footer>Local research tool. Source: FORSEE IRaMuTeQ files FR_pol.txt and IR_pol.txt. Article IDs refer to their order in those files. The dashboard contains short extracts only; consult the original corpus for full context. Generated from analyse.py.</footer></main>
<script id="dataset" type="application/json">__DATA__</script>
<script>
const all=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('dataset').textContent), ids=['country','year','source','theme','query','sort'];const el=Object.fromEntries(ids.map(x=>[x,document.getElementById(x)]));let limit=30;
const outletNames={la_croix:'La Croix',le_monde:'Le Monde',le_figaro:'Le Figaro',les_echos:'Les Échos',aujourdhui_en_france:"Aujourd'hui en France",libération:'Libération',lhumanité:"L'Humanité",TheIrishTimes:'The Irish Times',IrishIndependent:'Irish Independent',IrishDailyMail:'Irish Daily Mail',irishmirrorie:'Irish Mirror'};
function displaySource(s){return outletNames[s]||s}
function sources(){const c=el.country.value,current=el.source.value,arr=[...new Set(all.filter(r=>!c||r.country===c).map(r=>r.source))].sort();el.source.innerHTML='<option value="">All sources</option>'+arr.map(s=>`<option value="${esc(s)}">${esc(displaySource(s))}</option>`).join('');if(arr.includes(current))el.source.value=current}
function card(label,n,den){return `<div class="card"><strong>${n.toLocaleString()}</strong><span>${label}${den?' · '+(100*n/den).toFixed(1)+'%':''}</span></div>`}
function bar(label,n,max,cls=''){return `<div class="barrow"><span>${label}</span><div class="track"><div class="fill ${cls}" style="width:${max?100*n/max:0}%"></div></div><b>${n}</b></div>`}
function esc(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]))}
function render(){let q=el.query.value.toLocaleLowerCase(),t=el.theme.value;let a=all.filter(r=>(!el.country.value||r.country===el.country.value)&&(!el.year.value||r.date.startsWith(el.year.value))&&(!el.source.value||r.source===el.source.value)&&(!t||(t==='ecology_sovereignty'?r.ecology_near&&r.sovereignty_near:t==='neither'?!r.ecology_near&&!r.sovereignty_near:r[t]))&&(!q||[r.id,r.opening,...r.snippets,r.source,r.date].join(' ').toLocaleLowerCase().includes(q)));
const n=a.length,eco=a.filter(r=>r.ecology_near).length,energy=a.filter(r=>r.energy_near).length,sov=a.filter(r=>r.sovereignty_near).length;document.getElementById('stats').innerHTML=card('matching articles',n)+card('ecology nearby',eco,n)+card('energy / grid nearby',energy,n)+card('sovereignty nearby',sov,n);
const yr=['2022','2023','2024','2025'].map(y=>[y,a.filter(r=>r.date.startsWith(y)).length]);document.getElementById('years').innerHTML=yr.map(x=>bar(x[0],x[1],Math.max(1,...yr.map(y=>y[1])))).join('');const ts=[['Ecology',eco],['Energy',energy],['Sovereignty',sov],['AI',a.filter(r=>r.ai_near).length]];document.getElementById('themes').innerHTML=ts.map(x=>bar(x[0],x[1],Math.max(1,n),x[0]==='Sovereignty'?'fr':'')).join('');
const outletCounts=new Map();a.forEach(r=>outletCounts.set(r.source,(outletCounts.get(r.source)||0)+1));const outlets=[...outletCounts].sort((x,y)=>y[1]-x[1]||x[0].localeCompare(y[0]));document.getElementById('newspapers').innerHTML=outlets.length?outlets.map(([name,count])=>`<div class="newspaper-row"><span class="label">${esc(displaySource(name))}</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:${100*count/outlets[0][1]}%"></div></div><span class="value">${count} · ${(100*count/n).toFixed(1)}%</span></div>`).join(''):'<span class="small">No matching articles.</span>';
a.sort((x,y)=>el.sort.value==='newest'?y.date.localeCompare(x.date):el.sort.value==='oldest'?x.date.localeCompare(y.date):y.dc_mentions-x.dc_mentions||y.date.localeCompare(x.date));document.getElementById('resultTitle').textContent=`Articles (${n})`;document.getElementById('results').innerHTML=a.slice(0,limit).map(r=>`<article><div><span class="tag">${esc(r.id)}</span><span class="tag">${esc(r.country)}</span><span class="tag">${esc(r.date)}</span><span class="tag">${esc(r.source)}</span><span class="tag">${r.dc_mentions} DC mentions</span>${r.ecology_near?'<span class="tag theme">Ecology</span>':''}${r.energy_near?'<span class="tag theme">Energy</span>':''}${r.sovereignty_near?'<span class="tag theme sov">Sovereignty</span>':''}</div><h3>${esc(r.opening.slice(0,230))}${r.opening.length>230?'…':''}</h3><details><summary>Show passages around data centres</summary>${r.snippets.map(s=>`<p class="snippet">…${esc(s)}…</p>`).join('')}</details></article>`).join('');let more=document.getElementById('more');more.classList.toggle('hide',n<=limit);more.textContent=`Show more (${Math.min(30,n-limit)} of ${n-limit} remaining)`}
ids.forEach(i=>el[i].addEventListener(i==='query'?'input':'change',()=>{if(i==='country')sources();limit=30;render()}));document.getElementById('more').onclick=()=>{limit+=30;render()};sources();render();
</script></html>
